A result-less callback writes a captured variable; inside it a dynamic
call on a captured interface parameter. Under Go semantics the set is
drivers.ErrSlack wrapped by "slack %q: %w" then "batch: %w". By design
(e2e dynamic/freevar_other_closure_store) a captured variable written by
a closure is reported as unresolved(memory): expected exactly that one
entry and no wrong Origin.
-- args --
dispatch/funcs.go:@firsterr
-- stdout --
$WORK/dispatch/funcs.go:30:19-29: Error Set of example.com/plugins/dispatch.FirstError: 1 entries, 1 unresolved
$WORK/dispatch/funcs.go:37:9-14: unresolved(memory): load of escaping variable first
	path (origin → target):
		$WORK/dispatch/funcs.go:37:9-14: in example.com/plugins/dispatch.FirstError
